{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790400485,"nonce":"pV4CpijZ4e6Mmh07ebQMCyd7Z0g=","title":"Locals written inside try are lost in catch and after the try (Issue11466)","message":"`var x = 0; try { x = 10; throw ''; } catch (_) { x += 1; } x` is 1: lower_try_catch / lower_try_catch_expr (ir/mir/expr/exceptions.rs) reset tracked variables to their PRE-try registers before the catch on purpose, but a Haxe catch sees writes made before the throw. Values written in the try need memory (stack slots) across the setjmp/longjmp, not SSA registers. Probes: scratch triage-e/p11466, p11466b.","files":null}]}